    description: "WHAT (as reported)\nThe static test-coverage estimate reads far below what a user expects on some repositories: 17% for Flask, 4% for Express (37% for ripgrep, which the reviewer found believable). The output does say that tests reaching code indirectly are not counted; the reviewer's point is that the headline number misleads.\n\nASKED\nNot a number to \"fix\" by tuning: decide how the figure is labelled, or whether it is shown when the indirect share is large.\n\nREPORTED, NOT RE-RUN. Source: an outside reviewer who tried hypergumbo 10.0.0 from PyPI on 2026-11-24 (transcript pasted by the owner in session). Nothing in this item was run on dev by the filing agent unless a line says so; the reviewer's fixtures are not on this machine. FIRST STEP: reproduce on current dev with a fixture, and check the unreleased changelog, before building anything. Filed at the owner's request (\"file them all now\")."  # 9f35
